    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk it just feels so weirdly random sometimes. like, everything looks fine on my end, then i check a different network and it's totally different. is there any way to see where exactly the bottleneck is happening? like can i track the request as it moves through the different nodes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can trace these requests using tools like the Cloudflare \"Arrow UI\" or minehost DNS tracing to visualize where the old IP is being cached before reaching the user. Unfortunately, you typically cannot pin down a single specific bottleneck in the middle of the global network because the path your request takes varies depending on the user's physical location and which ISP handles the first hop. Once the system caches the data at a node, it acts as a mirror, making it mathematically impossible to force that specific node to update without waiting for its configured timeout.",
      "source": "target",
